# .clangd: the clangd configuration of the tree.
#
# `sh tools/dev/gen_compile_commands.sh` writes compile_commands.json (which
# git ignores) at the repository root; clangd reads it for each file's compile
# flags. The kernel and the guest programs are built with the i686-elf cross
# GCC, so clangd has to use that toolchain's headers (<stddef.h>, <stdint.h>
# and the rest) and builtins, not the host's. clangd asks the compiler named
# in the database for them, but only a driver it is allowed to run, so start
# clangd with:
#
#     --query-driver=**/i686-elf-*gcc
#
# (VS Code: set "clangd.arguments" to ["--query-driver=**/i686-elf-*gcc"]; other
# editors have an equivalent. See "The compilation database" in tools/Readme.md.)
#
# For the cross-compiled trees the driver is set to the i686-elf cross GCC, so
# that clangd uses its freestanding headers even before the database is made.
# The krffs host tools keep the host compiler's flags from the database.
If:
  PathMatch: [rach2/.*, tests/.*, ish/.*, utils/.*]
CompileFlags:
  Compiler: i686-elf-gcc
